---
import Container from "../Container.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../SectionHeading.astro";
import JoinCard from "../JoinCard.astro";
import MiniCalendar from "../MiniCalendar.astro";
import OpenGroupSignupForm from "../OpenGroupSignupForm.astro";
import { getNextOpenSession } from "../../data/sessions";
import { formatSessionLabel } from "../../lib/berlin-time";

const nextSession = getNextOpenSession();
const nextSessionLabel = nextSession ? formatSessionLabel(nextSession.date) : null;
---

<Container>
	<SectionHeading title="Two ways to join" id="join" />
	<p class="text-lg text-solarized-textSecondary mt-6 mb-8">
		Both groups do the same thing. The difference is who's in the room.
	</p>
	<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8">
		<JoinCard
			title="The open group"
			note="Free, no application, no commitment."
			cadence="Second and fourth Wednesday of the month"
			time="19:00 Berlin · 11:00 San Francisco"
		>
			{
				nextSession && nextSessionLabel && (
					<Fragment slot="cta">
						<OpenGroupSignupForm sessionDate={nextSession.date} sessionLabel={nextSessionLabel} />
					</Fragment>
				)
			}
			<MiniCalendar
				slot="calendar"
				startIndex={0}
				months={[
					{ label: "August", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 5, highlighted: [12, 26] },
					{ label: "September", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 30, startWeekday: 1, highlighted: [9, 23] },
					{ label: "October", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 3, highlighted: [14, 28] },
					{ label: "November", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 30, startWeekday: 6, highlighted: [11, 25] },
					{ label: "December", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 1, highlighted: [9, 23] },
					{ label: "January", year: 2027, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 4, highlighted: [13, 27] },
				]}
			/>
			<p>
				Come once to see what it's like, come every time, or come back after a few months away. The
				group is different every session, which keeps it easy to walk into.
			</p>
		</JoinCard>
		<JoinCard
			title="The closed group"
			note="Starting Wednesday, September 16, running for 3 months — 6 sessions in total."
			cadence="First and third Wednesday of the month"
			time="19:00 Berlin · 11:00 San Francisco"
			ctaLabel="Apply for the next cycle →"
			ctaHref="https://forms.gle/7hN2vLpKqRsTuVw29"
			footnote="Applications close September 9. I'll get back to everyone either way."
		>
			<MiniCalendar
				slot="calendar"
				startIndex={0}
				months={[
					{ label: "September", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 30, startWeekday: 1, highlighted: [16] },
					{ label: "October", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 3, highlighted: [7, 21] },
					{ label: "November", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 30, startWeekday: 6, highlighted: [4, 18] },
					{ label: "December", year: 2026, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 1, highlighted: [2] },
					{ label: "January", year: 2027, daysInMonth: 31, startWeekday: 4, highlighted: [] },
					{ label: "February", year: 2027, daysInMonth: 28, startWeekday: 0, highlighted: [] },
				]}
			/>
			<p>
				Same group of people the whole way through. That's the whole point: when you sit with the
				same faces every two weeks, you stop introducing yourself and start going somewhere. Things
				come up in session five that wouldn't have come up in session one.
			</p>
		</JoinCard>
	</div>
	<p class="text-center text-solarized-textSecondary mt-8">
		<strong class="text-solarized-textHeading">Not sure?</strong> Come to an open session first. Most
		people find it easier to decide once they've done it once.
	</p>
	<p class="text-center text-solarized-textSecondary mt-4">
		Both groups are free to join. The open group has no cost at all; the closed group carries a
		voluntary contribution of €25–100 for the cycle, entirely separate from applying — see
		<a href="/support">Support</a> for details.
	</p>
</Container>
